WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.685
"Side Effects of Water Fluoridation: Dental Fluorosis"

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.780
Fluoride research
over a half century

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.180
has historically established
water fluoridation to be safe

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.460
when used at typical
fluoridation doses

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.840
of one part per million.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.360
However, naturally
fluoridated waters

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.920
up around two parts per million

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.380
can put children
under the age of nine

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.900
at increased risk
for dental fluorosis,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.140
and a lifetime of drinking water
at four ppm can cause

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.900
skeletal fluorosis and increase
the risk of bone fractures.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.380
You can see these kinds of
levels in the Earth's natural

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.620
fluoride belts that extend
from Turkey through Iraq, Iran,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.660
and Afghanistan
to China and Japan.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.740
The reason susceptibility
to dental fluorosis ends

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.760
at around eight years old

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.060
is that's when enamel
maturation is completed,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.940
before our final permanent teeth
finish erupting.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.500
After teeth are formed,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.200
dental fluorosis can no longer
develop or worsen.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.740
At one ppm, one part
per million of fluoride,

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.140
public health authorities
estimated that less than

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.000
10 percent of kids
would develop the condition,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.980
and only in its mildest forms.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.920
We've since learned that
the prevalence and severity

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.320
of fluorosis is much higher
than predicted.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.580
According to the CDC,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.160
about a third of American
children now have some form

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.480
of dental fluorosis,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.940
with about one in 30
experiencing

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.260
a moderate to severe case.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.220
This may reflect exposure
to multiple fluoride sources

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.620
not factored into
the original calculations.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.900
Now, most fluorosis is so mild
as to be hardly noticeable,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.300
taking the form
of white streaks or splotches

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.680
visible only to dentists

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.200
under the bright lights
of their exam chair.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.980
But serious cases can involve
severe pitting and discoloration

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.980
and present more than just
a cosmetic defect.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.100
For example, one study found
that children with severe cases

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.520
are more likely to be viewed by
their peers as less attractive,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.700
less careful, less clean,
less happy, less healthy,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.540
less intelligent, less kind,
less reliable, less social.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.560
Imagine what that could do
to a kid's self-esteem.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.280
Given the higher-than-expected
rates of fluorosis,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.440
in 2015,
the U.S. Public Health Service

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.320
reduced the recommended fluoride
concentration of drinking water

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.740
down to 0.7 ppm
across the board.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:21.420
Previously, levels were set at
up to 1.2 ppm in cooler areas

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.040
where people tend
to drink less water.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.400
This change would be estimated
to keep the percentage

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.040
of those developing fluorosis
of "aesthetic concern"

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.960
down to approximately
12 percent.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.980
In terms of other health
concerns, until recently,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.820
mainstream medicine's view might
have perhaps best been summed up

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.000
by the final statement in
an exhaustive report published

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.400
by Consumer Reports in 1978:

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.260
"The simple truth is that

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.360
there is no
scientific controversy

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.560
over the safety of fluoridation.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.320
The practice is safe,
economical, and beneficial.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.260
The survival
of this fake controversy,

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.700
in the Consumer Union's opinion,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.060
is one of the major triumphs
of quackery over science

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.140
in our generation."

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.140
In the last few years, though,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.080
there have been growing concerns
about the adverse effects

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.360
of fluoride
on brain development,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.780
which I'll address next.

